# Repository Structure Standard

Defines the canonical, streamlined layout so new files, docs, and modules land in the right place by default and the working tree stays clean. Full rationale and the layered `src/` map are in [docs/development/REPO-STRUCTURE.md](../../docs/development/REPO-STRUCTURE.md).

## Canonical layout

- **Repo root** holds only config + entry docs: `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `requirements*.txt`, `pyproject.toml`, and dotfiles. **No** release notes, logs, generated artifacts, or ad-hoc scratch files at root.
- `src/` — application code. New modules follow the layered map in `REPO-STRUCTURE.md` (pipeline / portmap / diagrams / advanced / web / utils). **Existing flat `src/` modules stay as-is** — the layered map is enforced for NEW modules only; a subpackage refactor of existing modules is a deferred backlog item.
- `tests/` — mirrors `src/`.
- `docs/` — all documentation, in its sub-homes: `deployment/`, `development/`, `api/`, `confluence/`, `marketing/`, `issues/<ID>/`, `releases/`.
- `config/` — runtime config (gitignored actuals; `*.template` committed).
- `packaging/`, `scripts/`, `frontend/`, `assets/`, `.github/`, `.cursor/` — as named.

## Fixed homes for pipeline artifacts

- `AGENTS.md` → repo root.
- Skills → `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`; hooks → `.cursor/hooks.json`; rules → `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`.
- Under `docs/`: `PROJECT-STATUS.md`, `TODO-ROADMAP.md`, `ROADMAP-ARCHIVE.md`, `PLANS-INDEX.md`, `DECISIONS.md`, `PIPELINE-METRICS.md`, `CHANGELOG-ARCHIVE.md`, `releases/RELEASE_NOTES_v*.md`, `development/AGENTIC-CICD-PIPELINE.md`, `development/REPO-STRUCTURE.md`.

## Runtime / generated convention

- One documented, **gitignored** set: `logs/ output/ clusters/ reports/ import/ telemetry/ build/ dist/ test_output/ tracer-output/ archive/`.
- `scripts/clean-workspace.sh` purges them. No generated artifact is ever committed.
- `.archive/` (or `archive/`) is **gitignored and local-only** — content is retired here, never pushed.

## Enforcement

- `codebase-health` skill runs the recurring orphan / dead-file / duplication / drift sweep, proposing archival or consolidation with a diff for approval.
- A `.cursor/hooks.json` warning fires when a new file lands outside this standard (e.g. a new top-level file or a release note outside `docs/releases/`).
- New skills, agents, workflows, and docs adhere to this layout by default; `AGENTS.md` and the master pipeline doc reference it.
